// Preset logo-search window (ANDROID §6.4) — the modal card that assigns a
// station's logo, opened by the per-tile logo-search badge in reorder mode.
//
// It is the ONLY way a logo is ever assigned: there is no automatic or background
// fetch (§6.4, and the header comment on LogoSearchOverlay.tsx says the same). It
// also opens on a LANDING view, never straight into a search — the current logo
// plus the two per-station hero display toggles — and the search runs only when
// the Search button is pressed.
//
// FIVE BODIES, one at a time: landing (with a logo / without one), loading,
// results (the 2×2 grid), no-results, error. `saving` is not a sixth: Confirm
// spins while the results grid stays on screen underneath (the dc.html folds
// saving into `isResults`, LogoSearchOverlay.dc.html:187).
//
// WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. `LogoSearchOverlay.dc.html` is the built reference
// and §6.4 calls it "the exact reference", so it wins on appearance;
// `src/components/carfm/LogoSearchOverlay.tsx` is the shipping code and wins on
// behaviour. Every value below cites one of them by line. The places where the
// two disagree are called out where they bite rather than quietly resolved.
//
// DESIGN SIZE 720×560 IS NOT IN THE PROSE. §6's preamble lists design sizes for
// the numpad, the nearby picker and settings and simply omits this window. Both
// references state it and agree: the dc.html's `$preview` is {720, 560} and
// LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:47-48 caps at `Math.min(720, width − 32)` /
// `Math.min(560, height − 32)`. That TSX line is also the only one of the four
// overlays that implements §6's `screenW − 32dp` rule literally, which is where
// OverlayCard's 16px `edge-margin` came from in the first place.
//
// TYPE FLOORS. The references never ramp — a 13sp caption is 13sp on every
// surface. Carnyx ramps every design dimension through `Metrics.s()`, which at
// k = 0.68 would put that caption at 9px. Small type is therefore floored at 12px
// exactly the way `Metrics.pty-font`, `signal-num` and `stereo-font` already floor
// theirs (§10, "nothing critical below ~15sp"): the floor moves this file TOWARD
// the reference, not away from it. Hit targets floor at a real 48px for the same
// reason `CloseButton` and `NavButton` do.
//
// LETTER-SPACING STAYS RAW. `Metrics.s(0.3)` is `round(0.3 × k) × 1px` = 0px — the
// ramp destroys sub-pixel tracking. presets.slint (0.3/0.5) and status-bar.slint
// (1px) already keep theirs raw for the same reason.

import { Pal, Metrics } from "tokens.slint";
import { OverlayCard, OverlayHeader, OverlayFooter } from "overlay.slint";
import { VPath } from "icons.slint";

// ── Data the Rust side fills in ──────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Which of the five mutually exclusive bodies is showing.
///
/// An enum rather than the dc.html's five overlapping booleans (`isLanding`,
/// `isLoading`, `isResults`, `isEmpty`, `isError`), which can contradict each
/// other and are all derived from ONE upstream question — has a search been run,
/// did it return anything, did it throw. Rust answers it once.
///
/// `saving` is deliberately NOT a member: it is a separate flag, because the grid
/// stays visible underneath it (dc.html:187, `isResults = 'results' || 'saving'`).
export enum LogoSearchState {
    /// The window as it opens. Shows the current logo + display toggles, or the
    /// "No Logo Installed" message. `has-logo` picks between the two.
    landing,
    /// A search is in flight.
    loading,
    /// Four candidates to choose from. The only state with a grid.
    results,
    /// The search returned nothing — the references' `empty`. Named for what it
    /// means rather than for the absent array.
    no-results,
    /// The search threw, or a save failed. `error-title` / `error-body` carry
    /// which of the two, already worded.
    error,
    /// A logo has just been assigned, and this asks how it should look on the
    /// DARK face — the reference's `LogoDarkPicker`, which it mounts as its own
    /// modal over this window and which is folded into this one here.
    ///
    /// ONE MODAL AND NOT TWO, which is an architecture difference rather than a
    /// design one: this app has ONE overlay at a time (`Overlay` in app.slint),
    /// and the reference's picker is only ever opened from here, closes this
    /// window when it closes, and wears the same card. What it draws is the
    /// reference's: a swatch per treatment on the REAL dark surface, the
    /// pipeline's own choice badged AUTO, Skip and Use this in the footer.
    ///
    /// `dark-choices` EMPTY IN THIS STATE IS THE WAIT, not an empty answer.
    /// Building four treatments is seconds of pixel work on the logo worker; the
    /// reference spins an `ActivityIndicator` over the same pause, and this draws
    /// the same spinner `loading` does. An offer that comes back with nothing
    /// never reaches this state at all — Rust closes the window instead, because
    /// a picker with no answers is worse than none.
    dark-pick,
}

/// One dark treatment, already rendered, for the picker's swatch row.
///
/// THE ART IS ALREADY THE TREATMENT — recoloured, haloed, or left alone — and
/// composited by the swatch onto the same dark colour the face uses. `plated` is
/// the one that is not a finished picture: the `plate` treatment's PNG is a KEYED
/// MARK meant to sit on the grey `#E6E6E6` slab, and drawn without it that swatch
/// is a dark logo on a dark ground, which is the exact failure the treatment
/// exists to fix.
export struct DarkChoice {
    /// The rendered candidate, on transparency.
    art: image,
    /// "Recolor" / "Glow" / "As-is" / "Plate", worded in Rust.
    label: string,
    /// The pipeline's own choice. Badged, never auto-selected here — Rust decides
    /// which row opens selected, and it is the STORED one when there is one.
    auto: bool,
    /// Needs the grey slab behind it. See the struct note.
    plated: bool,
}

/// One image candidate, already fetched, already filtered, already formatted.
///
/// §6.4: "the first four image candidates". Rust filters to results whose image
/// URL matches `^https?://`, takes the first four IN ARRIVAL ORDER and re-sorts
/// nothing (services/logoDuckDuckGo.ts:82-84). Nothing here joins, rounds or
/// classifies anything.
export struct LogoCandidate {
    /// The thumbnail to draw. DDG's proxied thumbnail is what both references
    /// show (`r.thumbnail`, LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:269) — the full-size image is
    /// only fetched on Confirm, and frequently 403s.
    thumb: image,
    /// The registrable-ish host — "wikipedia.org", not "en.wikipedia.org" and not
    /// DDG's "Bing" provider label (logoDuckDuckGo.ts:53-58). Falls back to the
    /// literal "image" (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:279); Rust does that substitution,
    /// so an empty string here means an empty caption, not a bug to paper over.
    domain: string,
    /// "512×512" with U+00D7 MULTIPLICATION SIGN, or EMPTY when either dimension
    /// is missing. Formatted per cell in Rust — Slint's float-to-string has no
    /// precision control and no way to pick a separator.
    dims: string,
    /// §6.4: "the candidate art on its own background". The dc.html gives every
    /// cell its own `imgBg` (dc.html:209); the TSX hard-codes '#FFFFFF'
    /// (styles.imgWrap:420). The prose backs the dc.html, so this is a per-
    /// candidate colour Rust must derive from the art (sample the corner, or fall
    /// back to white — which is what the shipping build effectively does).
    background: color,
    /// "Logo option 3 from wikipedia.org", already assembled — the " from …" half
    /// is dropped when the domain is empty (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:266). A screen
    /// reader label is still a formatted string, so Rust builds it.
    alt: string,
}

// ── Icons ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Magnifier over a picture — the empty/no-logo mark (dc.html `emptyGlyph`:258).
///
/// Five parts: a rounded frame, a sun, a hill, the lens and its handle. The SVG's
/// `<rect x=3 y=4 width=14 height=12 rx=2>` is written out as the arc-cornered
/// subpath it compiles to; `<circle>` becomes the two-arc idiom already used
/// throughout icons.slint.
///
/// DISAGREEMENT, resolved for the dc.html. It uses this ONE glyph for both the
/// landing-no-logo view and the no-results view. LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:228-232
/// draws only the first THREE parts on landing — frame, sun, hill, no lens and no
/// handle — and the full five at :290-296. The dc.html wins on appearance, so both
/// states get all five; the landing view keeps the dc's 0.85 container opacity
/// (`noLogoGlyphStyle`:275), which the no-results view does not have.
///
/// This is NOT the §6.4 trigger badge's glyph. That one (icons.tsx:327-337) is a
/// different drawing at a different weight — 12×10 frame, a FILLED sun, a 4.2
/// lens, stroke 2 — and it lives with the preset band, not here.
component PictureLens {
    in property <length> size: 46px;
    in property <color> color;

    width: root.size;
    height: root.size;

    VPath {
        box-w: root.size; box-h: root.size; vbw: 24; vbh: 24; raw-stroke: 1.8;
        commands: "M5 4 H15 A2 2 0 0 1 17 6 V14 A2 2 0 0 1 15 16 H5 A2 2 0 0 1 3 14 V6 A2 2 0 0 1 5 4 Z M6.1 8.5 A1.4 1.4 0 1 0 8.9 8.5 A1.4 1.4 0 1 0 6.1 8.5 Z M3.5 14 L8 9.5 L12 13 M13 17 A4 4 0 1 0 21 17 A4 4 0 1 0 13 17 Z M20 20 L22.5 22.5";
        stroke: root.color;
        stroke-line-cap: round;
        stroke-line-join: round;
    }
}

/// The plain lens on the query chip row (dc.html `queryIcon`:252).
///
/// Deliberately NOT the §7 magnifier-over-tower and NOT the picture-lens above:
/// three different magnifiers do three different jobs in this design, and §6.4 is
/// explicit that the logo mark must be distinguishable from the Nearby one.
component QueryLens {
    in property <length> size: 16px;
    in property <color> color;

    width: root.size;
    height: root.size;

    VPath {
        box-w: root.size; box-h: root.size; vbw: 24; vbh: 24; raw-stroke: 2.2;
        commands: "M4 11 A7 7 0 1 0 18 11 A7 7 0 1 0 4 11 Z M20.5 20.5 L16.65 16.65";
        stroke: root.color;
        stroke-line-cap: round;
        stroke-line-join: round;
    }
}

/// The white check, on the option checkboxes and on the selected cell's badge
/// (dc.html `checkIcon`:255 — polyline "5 12.5 10 17.5 19 6.5").
///
/// The ONLY mark that carries selection state in this window. §6 and §6.4 both
/// restate the colourblind rule: blue fill and this check, never red or green.
///
/// It has to be drawn rather than typed. U+2713/U+2714 are absent from BOTH
/// bundled Atkinson cuts (I read the cmaps of ui/fonts/AtkinsonHyperlegible-
/// {Regular,Bold}.ttf: · × … ' — are present; ✓ ✕ ★ ⚠ are not), and the software
/// renderer that produces our screenshots has no fallback stack to lean on.
component CheckMark {
    in property <length> size: 17px;
    in property <color> color;

    width: root.size;
    height: root.size;

    VPath {
        box-w: root.size; box-h: root.size; vbw: 24; vbh: 24; raw-stroke: 3;
        commands: "M5 12.5 L10 17.5 L19 6.5";
        stroke: root.color;
        stroke-line-cap: round;
        stroke-line-join: round;
    }
}

/// The error mark (dc.html `errorGlyph`:262).
///
/// NOT icons.slint's `WarningTriangle`. That one is the Feather glyph — rounded
/// corners baked into the path, stroke 2, and a "M12 17 L12.01 17" dot. This one
/// is a sharp-cornered triangle at stroke 1.9 with a real filled dot, and the two
/// are visibly different marks. Amber is the fixed §3 safety colour and is right
/// here; it is not part of the accent system and never themes.
component ErrorTriangle {
    in property <length> size: 46px;
    in property <color> color;

    width: root.size;
    height: root.size;

    VPath {
        box-w: root.size; box-h: root.size; vbw: 24; vbh: 24; raw-stroke: 1.9;
        commands: "M12 3 L22 20 H2 Z M12 9.5 L12 14.5";
        stroke: root.color;
        stroke-line-cap: round;
        stroke-line-join: round;
    }
    // The dot is `<circle r=0.6 fill stroke>` — filled AND stroked at the svg's
    // 1.9, so it renders about 3.1 units across. Separate because one Path cannot
    // fill one subpath and not the others.
    VPath {
        box-w: root.size; box-h: root.size; vbw: 24; vbh: 24; raw-stroke: 1.9;
        commands: "M11.4 17.4 A0.6 0.6 0 1 0 12.6 17.4 A0.6 0.6 0 1 0 11.4 17.4 Z";
        fill: root.color;
        stroke: root.color;
    }
}

/// The busy ring — 44dp on the loading view, 18dp inside Confirm while saving
/// (dc.html `spinnerStyle`:297 and `confirmSpinnerStyle`:307, both 0.8s linear
/// infinite).
///
/// Slint ships no spinner, and the dc's is a CSS border trick with no direct
/// equivalent: a full ring in the track colour with `border-top-color` swapped for
/// the accent, rotated. So the track is a bordered Rectangle and the leading
/// quarter is a Path arc whose ENDPOINTS move.
///
/// WHY NOT JUST ROTATE IT. `rotation-angle` exists on Image and Text but not on
/// Path (i-slint-compiler-1.17.1/builtins.slint:375, 561; the Path at 2288 has
/// none), and the `transform-rotation` reserved property that IS available on
/// every element (typeregister.rs:234) is dropped by the SOFTWARE renderer —
/// its `current_transform` returns a translation and nothing else
/// (i-slint-renderer-software-1.17.1/lib.rs:3125-3127). A transform-spun ring
/// would sit frozen on every software-rendered surface. Moving the endpoints is
/// correct on both renderers.
///
/// Math.sin/Math.cos do exist (i-slint-compiler-1.17.1/lookup.rs:797-798), and
/// path ELEMENTS keep their bindings as live expressions rather than being folded
/// to a constant (passes/compile_paths.rs:95-105), which is what makes a moving
/// arc possible at all. icons.slint's header note that Slint has "no trig" is out
/// of date; what it does not have is loops and stroke-dasharray.
component SpinnerRing inherits Rectangle {
    in property <length> size: 44px;
    /// Ring thickness — 4 at 44dp, 3 at 18dp.
    in property <length> ring: 4px;
    in property <color> track;
    in property <color> arc;

    width: root.size;
    height: root.size;

    // 0 → 360 forever. `animate` only runs on a CHANGE, so `init` supplies one —
    // the same shape status-bar.slint's `Tell` uses to start its TA pulse.
    property <angle> spin: 0deg;
    init => { self.spin = 360deg; }
    animate spin { duration: 800ms; easing: linear; iteration-count: -1; }

    // Arc radius in viewbox units, inset by half the stroke so the ring's OUTER
    // edge lands on the box — which is where a CSS `border` on a 50%-radius box
    // puts it, and the track below is drawn exactly that way.
    property <float> r: 50 - 50 * root.ring / root.size;

    Rectangle {
        width: root.size;
        height: root.size;
        border-radius: root.size / 2;
        border-width: root.ring;
        border-color: root.track;
    }

    Path {
        // VPath's correction, applied by hand: VPath takes `commands`, and this
        // arc has to be built from path ELEMENTS because its endpoints move every
        // frame. Same arithmetic — the geometry is fitted into (element − stroke)
        // and offset by stroke/2, and stroke-width is not scaled by the viewbox.
        viewbox-x: 0;
        viewbox-y: 0;
        viewbox-width: 100;
        viewbox-height: 100;
        x: 0px - root.ring / 2;
        y: 0px - root.ring / 2;
        width: root.size + root.ring;
        height: root.size + root.ring;
        stroke: root.arc;
        stroke-width: root.ring;

        MoveTo {
            x: 50 + root.r * Math.cos(root.spin);
            y: 50 + root.r * Math.sin(root.spin);
        }
        // A quarter turn, clockwise in screen coordinates (y grows downward, so
        // an increasing angle IS clockwise and `sweep` is true). 90° is what
        // `border-top-color` on a circle paints.
        ArcTo {
            x: 50 + root.r * Math.cos(root.spin + 90deg);
            y: 50 + root.r * Math.sin(root.spin + 90deg);
            radius-x: root.r;
            radius-y: root.r;
            sweep: true;
        }
    }
}

// ── Pieces of the window ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// The square in the header: the station's real logo, or its monogram cube.
///
/// TWO renderings, and the split is the same one PlateBox makes in presets.slint.
/// With a logo the plate is transparent and the image is contained INSIDE it — the
/// plate owns the geometry, which is what keeps a wide wordmark or a tall lockup
/// from overflowing (§4.5's containment invariant, LogoTile.tsx:451-460). Without
/// one it is a solid cube in the hashed station colour with a white monogram
/// (LogoTile.tsx:466-483).
///
/// DISAGREEMENT, split. The dc.html only ever draws the cube — it has no image
/// loader — so it hard-codes the monogram at `narrow ? 16 : 19` with 0.5 tracking
/// (dc.html:279). The TSX draws the real logo when there is one and derives the
/// monogram size as `round(box × (len > 3 ? 0.26 : 0.34))`, with no tracking.
/// Behaviour is the TSX's, so a real logo wins; the derived size is kept because
/// it EQUALS the dc's hard-coded 19 and 16 at 56dp and 48dp for the ≤3-character
/// case and, unlike the constant, still fits four letters. The 0.5 tracking is the
/// dc's and is kept — presets.slint's CallSignBox tracks its letters the same way.
component StationTile inherits Rectangle {
    in property <image> logo;
    in property <bool> has-logo: false;
    /// The ≤4-character monogram, already reduced in Rust (tokens.ts `monogram`:
    /// upper-case, split on '-', a leading K/W dropped from a 4-letter base).
    in property <string> mono;
    in property <color> brand;

    border-radius: Metrics.s(14);
    clip: true;
    background: root.has-logo ? transparent : Pal.flat(root.brand);

    if root.has-logo: Image {
        source: root.logo;
        image-fit: contain;
        width: parent.width;
        height: parent.height;
        // LIMIT OF THE §4.7 DEAD FACE, as noted on presets.slint's PlateBox: the
        // palette's desaturation cannot reach an image, so a released-audio face
        // still shows logo art in full colour. The fix is a desaturated variant at
        // load time, not a filter Slint does not have.
    }
    if !root.has-logo: Text {
        text: root.mono;
        color: Pal.flat(#FFFFFF);
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.5px;
        // Branching on the string's own length, which is what presets.slint's
        // CallSignBox already does to fit its call letters. This reads a length,
        // it does not decide anything: the monogram itself arrived finished.
        font-size: Math.round(root.width / 1px
            * (root.mono.character-count > 3 ? 0.26 : 0.34)) * 1px;
    }
}

/// One of the two landing-view display rows, "Display Call Sign" and "Display
/// Frequency" (dc.html `optRowStyle`:272, TSX `styles.optRow`:407).
///
/// §6.4: these affect the HERO CARD ONLY. They never touch preset tiles, peek
/// cards or Nearby, they are saved per station, and a freshly-assigned logo
/// forces both OFF so the hero is logo-only.
///
/// The height is a MINIMUM. The dc reaches ~52 through 13dp of vertical padding
/// and the TSX states `minHeight: 52` outright; §10 requires ×1.5 font scale
/// without overlap, so it has to be able to grow. The 48px floor under it is §10's
/// hit-target rule in real dp, as on CloseButton.
component OptionRow inherits Rectangle {
    in property <string> label;
    in property <bool> checked: false;

    callback toggled();

    min-height: Math.max(48px, Metrics.s(52));
    border-radius: Metrics.s(12);
    border-width: 1px;
    border-color: Pal.border;
    background: Pal.raised;
    opacity: touch.pressed ? 0.7 : 1.0;

    accessible-role: checkbox;
    accessible-label: root.label;
    accessible-checkable: true;
    accessible-checked: root.checked;

    touch := TouchArea { clicked => { root.toggled(); } }

    HorizontalLayout {
        padding-left: Metrics.s(18);
        padding-right: Metrics.s(18);
        padding-top: Metrics.s(13);
        padding-bottom: Metrics.s(13);
        spacing: Metrics.s(14);

        VerticalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            horizontal-stretch: 0;
            // 26dp box, 7dp corner, a 2dp border. OFF is the border colour on no
            // fill; ON is blue on blue — the check is carried by the fill alone,
            // never by a hue change (§6's colourblind rule).
            Rectangle {
                width: Metrics.s(26);
                height: Metrics.s(26);
                border-radius: Metrics.s(7);
                border-width: 2px;
                border-color: root.checked ? Pal.blue : Pal.border;
                background: root.checked ? Pal.blue : transparent;

                if root.checked: CheckMark {
                    // 17dp inside the 26dp box — the dc's shared `checkIcon`. The
                    // TSX draws 15 here and 17 on the result badge; the dc uses
                    // one mark at one size for both, and wins on appearance.
                    size: Metrics.s(17);
                    color: Pal.flat(#FFFFFF);
                }
            }
        }

        VerticalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            horizontal-stretch: 1;
            Text {
                text: root.label;
                font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(17));
                font-weight: 700;
                color: Pal.text;
                overflow: elide;
            }
        }
    }
}

/// The blue-outline action: "Search for a …" on the landing view and "Search
/// again" on the no-results / error views.
///
/// One component, two sizes, because the references give it two. The retry button
/// is genuinely SMALLER than the landing one — 48dp tall at 15sp against 54 at 16
/// (dc.html `retryStyle`:298 vs `searchBtnStyle`:274) — and both references agree
/// on both, so the difference is intended and not a rounding.
component AccentButton inherits Rectangle {
    in property <string> label;
    in property <length> button-height;
    in property <length> pad-h;
    in property <length> label-size;
    in property <length> corner;
    in property <length> tracking: 0px;

    callback clicked();

    min-height: Math.max(48px, root.button-height);
    // Wide enough for the label plus its side padding, whatever the label says —
    // "Search for a different logo" is a long string and neither reference gives
    // the button a width.
    min-width: label-text.preferred-width + 2 * root.pad-h;
    border-radius: root.corner;
    // 1.5, not 1: the accent buttons are a heavier weight than the neutral ones,
    // and it is a stroke weight, so it stays raw like every other hairline here.
    border-width: 1.5px;
    border-color: Pal.blue;
    background: Pal.blue-fill;
    opacity: touch.pressed ? 0.7 : 1.0;

    accessible-role: button;
    accessible-label: root.label;

    touch := TouchArea { clicked => { root.clicked(); } }

    label-text := Text {
        text: root.label;
        font-size: root.label-size;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: root.tracking;
        color: Pal.blue;
        horizontal-alignment: center;
    }
}

/// One dark-treatment swatch — the reference's `CandidateCard`.
///
/// THE WELL IS THE REAL DARK SURFACE, which is the whole idea of the control:
/// four thumbnails composited onto the colour the face actually uses, so a glance
/// answers a question a metric got wrong. `dark-bg` is handed down rather than
/// taken from `Pal`, because this can be open while the face is light.
///
/// THE PLATE TREATMENT DRAWS ITS SLAB, and only that one. Its PNG is a keyed mark
/// meant to sit on the grey `#E6E6E6` rounded rectangle the hero gives it; drawn
/// bare it is a dark logo on a dark ground, which is the failure the treatment
/// exists to fix. The reference sizes that slab at 78% of the well with 8dp of
/// inner padding, and the other three get 12dp of well padding instead.
///
/// SELECTED IS A 2dp BLUE EDGE, the same language `ResultCell` uses two
/// components up. AUTO is a separate mark from selected and they are often on
/// different rows — the picker opens on the STORED treatment, which is the
/// driver's own choice when they have made one.
component DarkSwatch inherits Rectangle {
    in property <DarkChoice> choice;
    in property <bool> selected: false;
    in property <color> dark-bg;
    in property <length> well-h;
    in property <length> caption-font;

    callback clicked();

    border-radius: Metrics.s(14);
    border-width: 2px;
    border-color: root.selected ? Pal.blue : Pal.border;
    clip: true;
    opacity: touch.pressed ? 0.85 : 1.0;

    accessible-role: button;
    accessible-label: root.choice.label + (root.choice.auto ? ", suggested" : "");

    touch := TouchArea { clicked => { root.clicked(); } }

    VerticalLayout {
        spacing: 0px;

        Rectangle {
            height: root.well-h;
            background: root.dark-bg;

            if !root.choice.plated: Image {
                x: Metrics.s(12);
                y: Metrics.s(12);
                width: parent.width - 2 * Metrics.s(12);
                height: parent.height - 2 * Metrics.s(12);
                source: root.choice.art;
                image-fit: contain;
            }

            if root.choice.plated: Rectangle {
                width: parent.width * 0.78;
                height: parent.height * 0.78;
                x: (parent.width - self.width) / 2;
                y: (parent.height - self.height) / 2;
                border-radius: Metrics.s(12);
                // The hero's own slab, and the one `LogoPlate.plate` draws.
                background: Pal.logo-plate;

                Image {
                    x: Metrics.s(8);
                    y: Metrics.s(8);
                    width: parent.width - 2 * Metrics.s(8);
                    height: parent.height - 2 * Metrics.s(8);
                    source: root.choice.art;
                    image-fit: contain;
                }
            }
        }

        Rectangle {
            background: Pal.raised;

            HorizontalLayout {
                padding: Metrics.s(8);
                spacing: Metrics.s(6);
                alignment: center;

                Text {
                    text: root.choice.label;
                    font-size: root.caption-font;
                    font-weight: 700;
                    color: Pal.text;
                    vertical-alignment: center;
                }

                Text {
                    text: "AUTO";
                    font-size: Math.max(9px, root.caption-font * 0.8);
                    font-weight: 700;
                    color: Pal.blue;
                    vertical-alignment: center;
                    // A GAUGE at zero opacity, so the label stays centred whether
                    // or not this row is the pipeline's pick.
                    opacity: root.choice.auto ? 1.0 : 0.0;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

/// One result cell (dc.html `cellStyle`:220 / `imgWrapStyle`:221 / `metaStyle`:224).
///
/// Single-select: tapping selects and deselects any other, and selecting is what
/// enables Confirm. Selected is 2dp blue on a blue tint plus the check badge —
/// blue only, never red or green (§6.4 restates §6's rule at exactly this control).
///
/// Absolutely positioned by the grid, so it takes its box rather than asking for
/// one; see the note on `cell-h` in the overlay.
component ResultCell inherits Rectangle {
    in property <LogoCandidate> candidate;
    in property <bool> selected: false;
    /// Floor for the art well — dc.html's `minHeight: narrow ? 58 : 70`.
    in property <length> well-min-h;
    in property <length> caption-font;
    in property <length> dims-font;

    callback clicked();

    border-radius: Metrics.s(16);
    border-width: root.selected ? 2px : 1px;
    border-color: root.selected ? Pal.blue : Pal.border;
    background: root.selected ? Pal.blue-fill : Pal.raised;
    opacity: touch.pressed ? 0.7 : 1.0;
    // dc.html transitions background and border over 0.12s ease. Only the colour
    // animates — the border WIDTH also changes, and animating that would move the
    // art inside the cell while the eye is on it.
    animate background, border-color { duration: 120ms; easing: ease; }

    accessible-role: button;
    accessible-label: root.candidate.alt;
    accessible-item-selectable: true;
    accessible-item-selected: root.selected;

    touch := TouchArea { clicked => { root.clicked(); } }

    VerticalLayout {
        padding: Metrics.s(8);
        spacing: Metrics.s(8);

        // The art well. It takes the cell's remaining height (dc's `flex: 1`),
        // which is what makes the grid's 1fr rows read as one block instead of
        // four content-sized boxes; the TSX's fixed 88dp is the simplification.
        well := Rectangle {
            vertical-stretch: 1;
            min-height: root.well-min-h;
            border-radius: Metrics.s(10);
            clip: true;
            // §6.4: "the candidate art on its own background". Per candidate, from
            // Rust — the TSX hard-codes white and loses the distinction.
            background: Pal.flat(root.candidate.background);

            // x/y stated, not defaulted. An Image is an implicit-size builtin, so
            // a child Image WITHOUT an x/y binding folds its SOURCE pixel size
            // into this Rectangle's layout info (compiler pass
            // default_geometry.rs:170 filters on exactly that binding, and
            // layout.rs:736's SkipNonImplicit lets an Image through where it skips
            // a Rectangle) — a 512×512 thumbnail would then demand a 512dp cell.
            // Positioning it explicitly takes it out of the measurement, which is
            // what `if`-wrapping does for the same Image in presets.slint.
            Image {
                x: 0;
                y: 0;
                source: root.candidate.thumb;
                image-fit: contain;
                width: parent.width;
                height: parent.height;
            }

            // dc.html's `inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,0,0,0.05)` — a hairline that keeps
            // a white-on-white logo from bleeding into a light cell. A border on
            // the well itself, since Slint has no inset shadow.
            Rectangle {
                border-radius: parent.border-radius;
                border-width: 1px;
                border-color: Pal.flat-a(#000000, 0.05);
            }

            if root.selected: Rectangle {
                // Inside the well at 8/8, so it sits ON the art rather than on the
                // cell — the reference positions it against `imgWrap`, not `cell`.
                // Reached by id: this element IS the conditional, and a repeated
                // element states its own geometry rather than inheriting a default.
                x: well.width - Metrics.s(28) - Metrics.s(8);
                y: Metrics.s(8);
                width: Metrics.s(28);
                height: Metrics.s(28);
                border-radius: self.width / 2;
                background: Pal.blue;
                // The dc's `0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.25)` is omitted: the software
                // renderer draws no shadow (draw_box_shadow is an empty TODO), and
                // the badge is legible without one — solid blue on the art.
                CheckMark {
                    size: Metrics.s(17);
                    color: Pal.flat(#FFFFFF);
                }
            }
        }

        // Caption: source domain left, pixel dimensions right.
        HorizontalLayout {
            padding-left: Metrics.s(4);
            padding-right: Metrics.s(4);
            spacing: Metrics.s(8);
            vertical-stretch: 0;

            Text {
                text: root.candidate.domain;
                font-size: root.caption-font;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: Pal.dim;
                horizontal-stretch: 1;
                // Elide is load-bearing, not decoration: an un-elided Text reports
                // its full width as its MINIMUM, and a long host would then refuse
                // to let the cell shrink and push the dimensions out of the cell.
                overflow: elide;
            }
            Text {
                text: root.candidate.dims;
                font-size: root.dims-font;
                font-weight: 400;
                color: Pal.dim;
                horizontal-stretch: 0;
                horizontal-alignment: right;
            }
        }
    }
}

/// Cancel and Confirm (dc.html `cancelBtnStyle`:303 / `confirmBtnStyle`:304).
///
/// Three paints, not two. ENABLED is a filled blue button with a 1.5dp blue edge
/// and white type. DISABLED is a 1dp neutral outline with dim type at 0.55.
/// SAVING keeps the disabled outline but at full opacity and adds the ring — that
/// odd combination is the dc's own (`opacity: saving ? 1 : 0.55`) and it is what
/// tells a held Confirm apart from a dead one.
component FooterButton inherits Rectangle {
    in property <string> label;
    in property <string> a11y-label;
    /// Cancel is the neutral one: no fill in any state, dim type, 1dp edge.
    in property <bool> primary: false;
    in property <bool> enabled: true;
    in property <bool> busy: false;
    in property <length> min-w;
    in property <length> button-height;

    callback clicked();

    property <bool> lit: root.primary && root.enabled && !root.busy;

    min-width: root.min-w;
    min-height: Math.max(48px, root.button-height);
    border-radius: Metrics.s(14);
    border-width: root.lit ? 1.5px : 1px;
    border-color: root.lit ? Pal.blue : Pal.border;
    background: root.lit ? Pal.blue : transparent;
    opacity: (root.enabled || root.busy)
        ? (touch.pressed && root.enabled ? 0.7 : 1.0)
        : 0.55;

    accessible-role: button;
    accessible-label: root.a11y-label;
    accessible-enabled: root.enabled;

    touch := TouchArea {
        // A held Confirm swallows its own taps, and a disabled one is not a
        // control at all — the reference passes `disabled` to the Pressable.
        enabled: root.enabled && !root.busy;
        clicked => { root.clicked(); }
    }

    HorizontalLayout {
        padding-left: Metrics.s(22);
        padding-right: Metrics.s(22);
        spacing: Metrics.s(10);
        alignment: center;

        if root.busy: VerticalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            SpinnerRing {
                size: Metrics.s(18);
                ring: Metrics.s(3);
                track: Pal.meter-empty;
                // The dc draws this ring in white-on-40%-white, which was written
                // for the BLUE-FILLED button — but `saving` takes the disabled
                // outline, so on a light card it would be a white ring on a near
                // white background, i.e. invisible. §10 makes legibility a safety
                // constraint, so the ring follows the label's own colour instead.
                // Flagged rather than copied: this is a contradiction inside the
                // reference, not a place where the TSX and the dc.html disagree.
                arc: root.lit ? Pal.flat(#FFFFFF) : Pal.dim;
            }
        }

        VerticalLayout {
            alignment: center;
            Text {
                text: root.label;
                font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(16));
                font-weight: 700;
                letter-spacing: 0.5px;
                color: root.lit ? Pal.flat(#FFFFFF) : Pal.dim;
            }
        }
    }
}

// ── The window ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

export component LogoSearchOverlay inherits Rectangle {
    // ── The station ──
    /// Display name, straight from the preset. The header title.
    in property <string> name;
    /// "{callsign}  ·  {freq} MHz", assembled in Rust. The callsign half plus its
    /// separator is included ONLY when the callsign is non-empty AND differs from
    /// the name (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:161); the frequency is always one decimal.
    /// The separator is TWO spaces, U+00B7, TWO spaces — not the single-spaced
    /// interpunct the Nearby rows use. All five characters are in the bundled
    /// Atkinson cuts, so this renders as written.
    in property <string> subtitle;
    /// The station's current logo. Drawn in the header tile and, on the landing
    /// view, large on its white plate.
    in property <image> logo;
    /// Whether that logo exists. It also picks between the two landing views, so
    /// there is one flag here and not two.
    in property <bool> has-logo: false;
    /// The monogram for the no-logo tile — tokens.ts `monogram`, already reduced.
    in property <string> mono;
    /// The station colour, hashed from the callsign in Rust (tokens.ts
    /// `brandColor`). Arrives finished; Slint still passes it through Pal.flat.
    in property <color> brand;

    // ── The search ──
    /// Which body is showing. `saving` is separate, below.
    in property <LogoSearchState> state: LogoSearchState.landing;
    /// The exact string that was searched, for the chip: "radio 98.1 wmgn logo".
    /// Built in Rust (logoDuckDuckGo.ts:23-27) — one decimal on the frequency, the
    /// callsign forced LOWER-CASE, whitespace collapsed, then trimmed, so a
    /// missing frequency yields "radio wmgn logo" and never junk. §6.4's reason
    /// for showing it at all is that the driver can trust the results.
    in property <string> query;
    /// Exactly the first four candidates, in arrival order.
    in property <[LogoCandidate]> candidates;
    /// Which cell is picked, or −1. Rust holds the selection, the way it holds the
    /// Nearby picker's genre — `pick()` reports the tap and nothing here toggles.
    in property <int> selected-index: -1;
    /// Confirm is held. The results grid stays on screen underneath and every
    /// control is inert until it resolves.
    in property <bool> saving: false;
    /// Which error, already worded. There are TWO: the dc.html's search failure
    /// ("Search couldn't finish" / "Something went wrong reaching the logo search.
    /// Check your connection and try again.") and a save failure the TSX adds at
    /// :305-312 ("Couldn't save that logo" / "Couldn't save this logo — {reason}.
    /// Try a different result.", em dash, reason interpolated). Rust picks and
    /// formats; the no-results copy below is fixed and is written inline.
    in property <string> error-title;
    in property <string> error-body;

    // ── The landing view ──
    /// The two hero display flags. Rust resolves them BEFORE the window opens:
    /// the saved per-station preference if there is one, else a logo-dependent
    /// default — a station WITH a logo defaults both OFF, which is §6.4's
    /// logo-only hero; a station without one defaults both ON
    /// (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:90).
    in property <bool> show-call: false;
    in property <bool> show-freq: false;
    /// "Search for a different logo" when a logo exists, "Search for a logo" when
    /// none does. A property and not a ternary here, because the copy is the
    /// reference's and belongs with the rest of the strings Rust owns.
    in property <string> search-label;

    // ── The footer ──
    /// `!saving && (landing || (results && a cell is picked))` (dc.html:231).
    in property <bool> can-confirm: false;
    /// "Save" on the landing view, "Confirm" in results, "Saving…" while saving.
    /// DISAGREEMENT: that three-way is the dc.html's (:247); the TSX hard-codes
    /// "Confirm" everywhere and, while saving, drops the label entirely for a bare
    /// spinner. The dc.html wins on appearance, so the label is always drawn and
    /// Rust supplies which of the three it is.
    in property <string> confirm-label;
    /// The footer hint — a five-way selection over (state, has-logo, can-confirm)
    /// yielding one of four strings or nothing, resolved in Rust:
    ///   landing + logo   "Display options apply to the main card"  (dc.html:248)
    ///                    "Choose what shows on the hero"           (TSX:329)
    ///   landing, no logo empty
    ///   confirmable      "Saved as this station's logo"
    ///   results, no pick "Pick the correct logo"
    ///   otherwise        empty
    /// DISAGREEMENT, unresolved: the two references word the first case
    /// differently and neither is obviously wrong — the dc.html is the exact
    /// reference, the TSX's wording matches §6.4's own name for the surface. It is
    /// one string either way, so the choice stays with Rust.
    in property <string> hint;
    /// The left footer button's label. "Cancel" everywhere but the dark picker,
    /// where the reference calls it "Skip" — and calls it that for a reason worth
    /// keeping: skipping is not cancelling. The logo is already saved by then and
    /// the auto-pick already stands; what the button declines is the question.
    in property <string> cancel-label: "Cancel";

    // ── The dark picker ──
    /// The treatments to choose between, already rendered. Empty in the
    /// `dark-pick` state means the adaptation is still running.
    in property <[DarkChoice]> dark-choices;
    /// The REAL dark surface the variants will sit on, handed over rather than
    /// read from `Pal`: this picker can be open while the face is LIGHT, and a
    /// swatch drawn on the light panel would be a preview of nothing. Rust reads
    /// it from the same constant the gate judged the candidates against.
    in property <color> dark-bg;

    // ── What the user can do ──
    /// A display row was tapped. Rust owns the flag and does the toggle.
    callback toggle-call();
    callback toggle-freq();
    /// The landing view's Search button — the ONLY thing that starts a search
    /// (§6.4: no query field, no submit).
    callback search();
    /// "Search again", from no-results or error. Separate from `search()` so Rust
    /// can tell the entry points apart: retry also clears the selection and the
    /// error before it runs (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:71).
    callback retry();
    /// A result cell was tapped. Single-select; Rust moves the selection.
    callback pick(int);
    callback confirm();
    /// The ✕, Cancel, and the scrim. All three close and change nothing (§6.4).
    callback close();

    // ── Per-instance metrics ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Everything below follows §6.2's width track, read off the RESOLVED card the
    // way Metrics.tall / .landscape / .two-rows are read off the surface. Both
    // references test the same threshold (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:49, `cardW < 620`),
    // which is exactly OverlayCard.narrow, so nothing here recomputes it.
    //
    // The narrow deltas, exhaustively — header padding and gap, the station tile,
    // the title, the query row's padding, the body's padding, the landing gap and
    // padding, the landing art's cap, the grid gap, the art well's floor, the
    // footer's padding, and the two footer buttons' width and height. NOTHING else
    // changes: the close button, the checkbox, the check badge, every radius, all
    // body typography and every string are identical on both tracks.
    property <length> body-pad-h: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 16 : 22);
    property <length> body-pad-top: Metrics.s(4);
    // dc.html's `bodyStyle` bottom is narrow ? 8 : 10; the TSX uses 10 on both.
    // One dp on one track, taken from the reference.
    property <length> body-pad-bottom: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 8 : 10);

    property <length> landing-pad-h: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 18 : 34);
    /// Width available to the landing column's own children, derived from the
    /// resolved card rather than read back off a layout — reading a layout's width
    /// and feeding it into that layout's children is the loop this codebase has
    /// already hit twice.
    property <length> landing-w: Math.max(0px,
        card.card-w - 2 * root.body-pad-h - 2 * root.landing-pad-h);

    property <length> center-pad-h: Metrics.s(40);
    property <length> center-w: Math.max(0px,
        card.card-w - 2 * root.body-pad-h - 2 * root.center-pad-h);
    /// dc.html `centerSubStyle.maxWidth`. The paragraph wraps inside it.
    property <length> center-sub-w: Math.min(Metrics.s(420), root.center-w);

    // ── The landing plate ──
    //
    // dc.html:269-270: a white plate that WRAPS the art — `padding: 14px 22px`,
    // `maxWidth: 82%`, and an image at `maxHeight: narrow ? 112 : 148` with
    // `width/height: auto`, so the plate is exactly as big as the logo needs.
    // (The TSX ships a fixed 70%-wide, 320-capped, 120-tall box with no ring
    // instead — a different sizing model, a different radius and a missing ring.
    // The dc.html is the reference and wins on appearance.)
    //
    // "Auto" needs the art's own aspect ratio, which `image.width`/`image.height`
    // supply (i-slint-compiler-1.17.1/lookup.rs:1097-1117). A missing or
    // still-unloaded image reports 0, so the ratio falls back to square rather
    // than dividing by it.
    property <length> plate-pad-h: Metrics.s(22);
    property <length> plate-pad-v: Metrics.s(14);
    property <length> plate-inner-w: Math.max(0px,
        Math.round(root.landing-w / 1px * 0.82) * 1px - 2 * root.plate-pad-h);
    property <float> logo-aspect: root.logo.height > 0
        ? root.logo.width / root.logo.height
        : 1.0;
    property <length> art-h: Math.min(Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 112 : 148),
        root.plate-inner-w / root.logo-aspect);
    property <length> art-w: root.art-h * root.logo-aspect;

    // ── The 2×2 grid ──
    //
    // dc.html:291 is a real grid: `1fr 1fr` by `1fr 1fr` with ONE gap on both
    // axes, so the four cells fill the band as a block. (The TSX is a wrapping
    // flex row of 48%-wide cells, which makes the column gap whatever 4% of the
    // width happens to be and leaves the cells content-tall. The dc.html is the
    // reference.) §6.4 requires it to fit the narrow track with NO horizontal
    // scroll, so the columns are derived from the band's width and only the
    // vertical axis can ever scroll.
    //
    // The cells are absolutely positioned inside the Flickable rather than laid
    // out, for the reason presets.slint's band gives: ids declared inside an `if`
    // are not visible outside it, and the arithmetic is trivial. The Flickable is
    // what cuts the loop — a child that reads its parent's height and reports that
    // height back as its own minimum is exactly the poison, and a Flickable's
    // layout info does not come from its viewport.
    property <length> grid-gap: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 10 : 14);
    property <length> grid-pad-h: Metrics.s(2);
    property <length> grid-pad-v: Metrics.s(6);
    property <length> well-min-h: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 58 : 70);
    property <length> caption-font: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(13));
    property <length> dims-font: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(12));
    /// The shortest a cell may be: 8dp padding, the art well's own floor, the 8dp
    /// gap, one caption line, 8dp padding. The caption is budgeted at 1.24× its
    /// font size, which is Atkinson's own line height (hhea ascender 950,
    /// descender −290 over a 1000 upem, in ui/fonts) — Slint cannot be asked for
    /// the height of an element it has not placed, and these cells are placed by
    /// hand.
    property <length> min-cell-h: 2 * Metrics.s(8) + root.well-min-h + Metrics.s(8)
        + Math.ceil(root.caption-font / 1px * 1.24) * 1px;
    property <length> band-w: Math.max(0px, body.width - 2 * root.body-pad-h);
    property <length> band-h: Math.max(0px,
        body.height - root.body-pad-top - root.body-pad-bottom);
    property <length> cell-w: Math.max(0px,
        (root.band-w - 2 * root.grid-pad-h - root.grid-gap) / 2);
    property <length> cell-h: Math.max(root.min-cell-h,
        (root.band-h - 2 * root.grid-pad-v - root.grid-gap) / 2);
    /// Two columns, so the row count is the candidate count halved and rounded up.
    /// Integer arithmetic here is float-based — `4 / 2` really is 2.0 — which is
    /// why the ceiling is explicit.
    property <int> grid-rows: Math.max(1, Math.ceil(root.candidates.length / 2));

    card := OverlayCard {
        width: root.width;
        height: root.height;
        // 720 × 560, capped to the surface less 32dp a side and centred. Corner,
        // card background and scrim all stay at their defaults: this overlay is
        // one of the three that use Pal.bg (dc.html `containerStyle`:266 and
        // LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:150); nothing wants Pal.panel since the numpad
        // card dissolved into the tune overlay's tab.
        design-width: 720;
        design-height: 560;
        // §6.4 lists the scrim beside Cancel and the ✕ as a way out, and it stays
        // one — except while a save is in flight, where the window is inert until
        // it resolves. Neither reference settles that case: the TSX's scrim has no
        // press handler at all (styles.scrim:376), so tapping outside does nothing
        // in the shipping build and there is no saving behaviour to copy.
        dismiss-on-scrim: !root.saving;
        close => { root.close(); }

        // ONE child, not four, for the reason the picker gives: the query band is
        // conditional, and a conditional element handed through another
        // component's @children is a shape nothing in this tree has compiled.
        // Keeping the conditionals in a layout declared HERE puts them in the same
        // scope as face.slint's and presets.slint's. The bands' own stretch
        // factors still decide who grows.
        VerticalLayout {

            // ── Header: station tile · name · callsign·freq · ✕ ──
            //
            // `head-height: 0` because this header is content-driven — the dc's
            // `headerStyle` has no height, only padding, and the tile is the
            // tallest thing in it. OverlayHeader's own 12dp spacing is the dc's
            // `gap: 12` between the left group and the ✕.
            OverlayHeader {
                head-height: 0px;
                pad-h: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 16 : 22);
                pad-v: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 14 : 16);
                close => { root.close(); }

                HorizontalLayout {
                    spacing: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 12 : 16);

                    VerticalLayout {
                        alignment: center;
                        horizontal-stretch: 0;
                        StationTile {
                            width: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 48 : 56);
                            height: self.width;
                            logo: root.logo;
                            has-logo: root.has-logo;
                            mono: root.mono;
                            brand: root.brand;
                        }
                    }

                    VerticalLayout {
                        alignment: center;
                        horizontal-stretch: 1;
                        spacing: Metrics.s(3);

                        Text {
                            text: root.name;
                            font-size: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 22 : 26);
                            font-weight: 700;
                            color: Pal.text;
                            // Both lines elide. An un-elided Text reports its full
                            // width as its minimum, so a long station name would
                            // refuse to shrink and push the ✕ off the card.
                            overflow: elide;
                        }
                        Text {
                            text: root.subtitle;
                            font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                            font-weight: 400;
                            letter-spacing: 0.3px;
                            color: Pal.dim;
                            overflow: elide;
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            // ── Query chip, every state except landing ──
            //
            // A SIBLING band between the header and the body, not a row inside it
            // (dc.html `queryRowStyle` carries `flexShrink: 0` and sits outside
            // `bodyStyle`), so the searched string never scrolls away with the
            // results. No rule and no fill of its own.
            //
            // AND NOT IN THE DARK PICKER, which is not a search state. What was
            // searched for is finished business by then — the logo is chosen and
            // saved — and the chip over that screen reads as a stale answer to a
            // question the driver has stopped being asked.
            if root.state != LogoSearchState.landing
                && root.state != LogoSearchState.dark-pick: Rectangle {
                vertical-stretch: 0;

                HorizontalLayout {
                    padding-left: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 16 : 22);
                    padding-right: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 16 : 22);
                    padding-top: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 10 : 12);
                    padding-bottom: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 10 : 12);
                    spacing: Metrics.s(10);
                    // Default (stretch) alignment on purpose: `alignment: start`
                    // would hand every child its preferred width and IGNORE the
                    // stretch factors, which is exactly the shrink the chip needs.

                    VerticalLayout {
                        alignment: center;
                        horizontal-stretch: 0;
                        QueryLens {
                            size: Metrics.s(16);
                            color: Pal.dim;
                        }
                    }

                    VerticalLayout {
                        alignment: center;
                        horizontal-stretch: 0;
                        Text {
                            // The dc.html holds "Searched" and upper-cases it in
                            // CSS; the TSX writes "SEARCHED" directly. Same
                            // rendered result, and Slint has no text-transform.
                            text: "SEARCHED";
                            font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(12));
                            font-weight: 700;
                            letter-spacing: 1.5px;
                            color: Pal.dim;
                        }
                    }

                    // The chip is the one thing in the row that shrinks. It takes
                    // the slack so it can be squeezed BELOW its content width on a
                    // narrow card, and `max-width` caps it at that content width so
                    // it never draws as an over-wide raised box — which is exactly
                    // what a CSS flex item with `flex-shrink: 1` does.
                    chip := Rectangle {
                        horizontal-stretch: 1;
                        max-width: query-text.preferred-width + 2 * Metrics.s(12);
                        border-radius: Metrics.s(8);
                        border-width: 1px;
                        border-color: Pal.border;
                        background: Pal.raised;

                        HorizontalLayout {
                            padding-left: Metrics.s(12);
                            padding-right: Metrics.s(12);
                            padding-top: Metrics.s(5);
                            padding-bottom: Metrics.s(5);
                            query-text := Text {
                                text: root.query;
                                font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                overflow: elide;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }

            // ── Body ──
            //
            // NOT OverlayBody. Three of the five bodies must be CENTRED in the
            // band and the results grid must FILL it, and OverlayBody's viewport is
            // its content's preferred height — which top-aligns short content and
            // gives a stretching child nothing to stretch into. So the band is
            // opened out here: the same Flickable-inside-a-Rectangle shape, with
            // the viewport floored at the band's own height so `alignment: center`
            // has slack to centre in and the grid has room to fill. Everything else
            // matches OverlayBody, scrollbar included — there isn't one, because
            // every reference hides its own.
            //
            // Two Flickables under two `if`s rather than one with the states
            // inside, because the column states need a content-measured viewport
            // (`col.preferred-height`) and the grid needs an arithmetic one, and an
            // id declared inside an `if` is not visible outside it.
            body := Rectangle {
                vertical-stretch: 1;
                min-height: 0px;

                // Landing / loading / no-results / error — a centred column.
                if root.state != LogoSearchState.results: Flickable {
                    x: root.body-pad-h;
                    y: root.body-pad-top;
                    width: root.band-w;
                    height: root.band-h;
                    // Vertical only: the viewport is exactly as wide as the band.
                    viewport-width: self.width;
                    // Floored at the band so a short body has slack to be centred
                    // in; taller content scrolls. Reads the content's PREFERRED
                    // height, never its resolved one.
                    viewport-height: Math.max(self.height, col.preferred-height);

                    col := VerticalLayout {
                        alignment: center;

                        // ── Landing, station HAS a logo ──
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.landing && root.has-logo: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 18 : 24);
                            padding-left: root.landing-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.landing-pad-h;
                            padding-top: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 8 : 10);
                            padding-bottom: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 8 : 10);

                            // The white plate. White is deliberate and is NOT a
                            // theme colour: logo art is composited on white in both
                            // themes because that is what the art expects. It still
                            // goes through Pal.flat — a no-op on white by
                            // construction, but no colour bypasses the function.
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                Rectangle {
                                    width: root.art-w + 2 * root.plate-pad-h;
                                    height: root.art-h + 2 * root.plate-pad-v;
                                    border-radius: Metrics.s(16);
                                    background: Pal.flat(#FFFFFF);
                                    // dc.html's `inset 0 0 0 1px t.border` — a real
                                    // 1dp ring, missing from the shipping TSX.
                                    border-width: 1px;
                                    border-color: Pal.border;

                                    // Placed by hand rather than centred by
                                    // default, for the reason spelled out on the
                                    // result cell's art: an Image with no x/y
                                    // binding folds its source pixel size into the
                                    // plate's layout info. The plate is exactly
                                    // the art plus its padding, so the offset IS
                                    // the padding.
                                    Image {
                                        x: root.plate-pad-h;
                                        y: root.plate-pad-v;
                                        source: root.logo;
                                        image-fit: contain;
                                        width: root.art-w;
                                        height: root.art-h;
                                    }
                                }
                            }

                            // The two hero display toggles.
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                VerticalLayout {
                                    // dc.html's `maxWidth: 400` (the TSX says 420
                                    // and puts it on the list rather than the row);
                                    // spacing 12 (the TSX says 10).
                                    width: Math.min(Metrics.s(400), root.landing-w);
                                    spacing: Metrics.s(12);

                                    OptionRow {
                                        label: "Display Call Sign";
                                        checked: root.show-call;
                                        toggled => { root.toggle-call(); }
                                    }
                                    OptionRow {
                                        label: "Display Frequency";
                                        checked: root.show-freq;
                                        toggled => { root.toggle-freq(); }
                                    }
                                }
                            }

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                AccentButton {
                                    label: root.search-label;
                                    button-height: Metrics.s(54);
                                    pad-h: Metrics.s(26);
                                    corner: Metrics.s(13);
                                    label-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(16));
                                    tracking: 0.3px;
                                    clicked => { root.search(); }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── Landing, NO logo ──
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.landing && !root.has-logo: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 18 : 24);
                            padding-left: root.landing-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.landing-pad-h;
                            padding-top: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 8 : 10);
                            padding-bottom: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 8 : 10);

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                PictureLens {
                                    size: Metrics.s(46);
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                    // dc.html `noLogoGlyphStyle` — this view's
                                    // glyph is at 0.85, the no-results one is not.
                                    opacity: 0.85;
                                }
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: "No Logo Installed";
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            Text {
                                // Curly apostrophe, U+2019 — in both bundled cuts.
                                text: "This station doesn’t have a logo yet.";
                                font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                font-weight: 400;
                                color: Pal.dim;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                AccentButton {
                                    label: root.search-label;
                                    button-height: Metrics.s(54);
                                    pad-h: Metrics.s(26);
                                    corner: Metrics.s(13);
                                    label-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(16));
                                    tracking: 0.3px;
                                    clicked => { root.search(); }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── Loading ──
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.loading: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(14);
                            padding-left: root.center-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.center-pad-h;

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                SpinnerRing {
                                    size: Metrics.s(44);
                                    ring: Metrics.s(4);
                                    // The dc's track is `t.track` — rgba(20,30,45,
                                    // 0.10) light / rgba(255,255,255,0.10) dark,
                                    // which is Pal.meter-empty exactly.
                                    track: Pal.meter-empty;
                                    arc: Pal.blue;
                                }
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: "Searching for logos…";
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                Text {
                                    width: root.center-sub-w;
                                    text: "Looking up brand art for this station.";
                                    font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    font-weight: 400;
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                    horizontal-alignment: center;
                                    wrap: word-wrap;
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── Dark picker: still adapting ──
                        //
                        // The same spinner `loading` draws, over a different
                        // wait: four treatments off one master, on the logo
                        // worker. `dark-choices` empty in this state IS the
                        // wait — an offer with nothing in it never reaches
                        // here, because Rust closes the window instead.
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.dark-pick && root.dark-choices.length == 0: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(14);
                            padding-left: root.center-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.center-pad-h;

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                SpinnerRing {
                                    size: Metrics.s(46);
                                    ring: Metrics.s(4);
                                    track: Pal.border;
                                    arc: Pal.blue;
                                }
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: "Adapting…";
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                Text {
                                    width: root.center-sub-w;
                                    text: "Working out how this logo should look on the dark theme.";
                                    font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    font-weight: 400;
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                    horizontal-alignment: center;
                                    wrap: word-wrap;
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── Dark picker: the treatments ──
                        //
                        // `LogoDarkPicker.tsx`: a title, one line of copy, then
                        // the candidates as a wrapping row of 150dp cards. The
                        // row wraps here too — four cards at 150 will not fit
                        // 360dp of phone — and the swatches are laid out by hand
                        // in a two-column grid on the narrow track for the same
                        // reason the results grid is.
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.dark-pick && root.dark-choices.length > 0: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(6);
                            padding-left: root.center-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.center-pad-h;
                            // TOP, NOT CENTRE. The wrapper this sits in centres
                            // its child, which is right for the four one-message
                            // bodies beside it and wrong for a list: a grid taller
                            // than the band would be centred and clipped at BOTH
                            // ends, losing the first row as well as the last.
                            alignment: start;

                            Text {
                                text: "Dark-mode logo";
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: "Pick how this logo looks on the dark theme. The suggested option is marked AUTO.";
                                font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(14));
                                font-weight: 400;
                                color: Pal.dim;
                                wrap: word-wrap;
                            }

                            grid := Rectangle {
                                // TWO COLUMNS ALWAYS, and the swatch takes what
                                // half the band gives it rather than the
                                // reference's fixed 150dp. Four fixed cards need
                                // 636dp with the gaps; the phone track's band is
                                // about 300. The reference wraps to two rows at
                                // that width anyway, so this is the same layout
                                // arrived at by measuring instead of by wrapping.
                                property <length> gap: Metrics.s(12);
                                // NOT `col`: Slint reserves `row`/`col`/`rowspan`/`colspan` on
                                // every element for GridLayout placement, and declaring
                                // one is 'Cannot override property'.
                                property <length> col-w: (self.width - self.gap) / 2;
                                property <length> well: Metrics.s(88);
                                property <length> cap: Metrics.s(30);
                                property <length> cell: self.well + self.cap;

                                // The swatches are placed by hand, so this is a
                                // plain Rectangle and not a layout — hence a
                                // measured height rather than padding, which has
                                // no effect on one.
                                property <length> lead: Metrics.s(10);
                                height: 2 * self.cell + self.gap + self.lead;

                                for c[i] in root.dark-choices: DarkSwatch {
                                    x: Math.mod(i, 2) * (grid.col-w + grid.gap);
                                    y: Math.floor(i / 2) * (grid.cell + grid.gap) + grid.lead;
                                    width: grid.col-w;
                                    height: grid.cell;
                                    choice: c;
                                    selected: i == root.selected-index;
                                    dark-bg: root.dark-bg;
                                    well-h: grid.well;
                                    caption-font: Math.max(11px, Metrics.s(14));
                                    clicked => { if (!root.saving) { root.pick(i); } }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── No results ──
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.no-results: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(14);
                            padding-left: root.center-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.center-pad-h;

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                PictureLens {
                                    size: Metrics.s(46);
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                }
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: "No logos found";
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                Text {
                                    width: root.center-sub-w;
                                    text: "The search came back empty. You can try again or keep the current monogram.";
                                    font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    font-weight: 400;
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                    horizontal-alignment: center;
                                    wrap: word-wrap;
                                }
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                // dc.html's `marginTop: 4` on the retry button, on
                                // top of the column's own 14dp gap.
                                padding-top: Metrics.s(4);
                                AccentButton {
                                    label: "Search again";
                                    button-height: Metrics.s(48);
                                    pad-h: Metrics.s(22);
                                    corner: Metrics.s(12);
                                    label-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    clicked => { root.retry(); }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // ── Error: the search threw, or a save failed ──
                        if root.state == LogoSearchState.error: VerticalLayout {
                            spacing: Metrics.s(14);
                            padding-left: root.center-pad-h;
                            padding-right: root.center-pad-h;

                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                ErrorTriangle {
                                    size: Metrics.s(46);
                                    color: Pal.amber;
                                }
                            }
                            Text {
                                text: root.error-title;
                                font-size: Metrics.s(22);
                                font-weight: 700;
                                color: Pal.text;
                                horizontal-alignment: center;
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                Text {
                                    width: root.center-sub-w;
                                    text: root.error-body;
                                    font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    font-weight: 400;
                                    color: Pal.dim;
                                    horizontal-alignment: center;
                                    wrap: word-wrap;
                                }
                            }
                            HorizontalLayout {
                                alignment: center;
                                padding-top: Metrics.s(4);
                                AccentButton {
                                    label: "Search again";
                                    button-height: Metrics.s(48);
                                    pad-h: Metrics.s(22);
                                    corner: Metrics.s(12);
                                    label-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(15));
                                    clicked => { root.retry(); }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ── Results: the 2×2 grid ──
                if root.state == LogoSearchState.results: Flickable {
                    x: root.body-pad-h;
                    y: root.body-pad-top;
                    width: root.band-w;
                    height: root.band-h;
                    // Horizontal scroll is forbidden by §6.4, and the viewport is
                    // exactly as wide as the band, so it cannot happen.
                    viewport-width: self.width;
                    viewport-height: root.grid-rows * root.cell-h
                        + (root.grid-rows - 1) * root.grid-gap
                        + 2 * root.grid-pad-v;

                    for c[i] in root.candidates: ResultCell {
                        x: Math.mod(i, 2) * (root.cell-w + root.grid-gap) + root.grid-pad-h;
                        y: Math.floor(i / 2) * (root.cell-h + root.grid-gap) + root.grid-pad-v;
                        width: root.cell-w;
                        height: root.cell-h;
                        candidate: c;
                        selected: i == root.selected-index;
                        well-min-h: root.well-min-h;
                        caption-font: root.caption-font;
                        dims-font: root.dims-font;
                        // A held Confirm ignores every input until it resolves.
                        clicked => { if (!root.saving) { root.pick(i); } }
                    }
                }
            }

            // ── Footer: hint · Cancel · Confirm ──
            //
            // `foot-height: 0` because this footer is content-driven — the dc's
            // `footerStyle` states padding only, and the 50/56dp buttons are the
            // tallest things in it. OverlayFooter's 16dp spacing is the dc's gap
            // between the hint and the button pair.
            OverlayFooter {
                foot-height: 0px;
                pad-h: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 16 : 22);
                pad-v: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 12 : 14);
                spacing: Metrics.s(16);

                VerticalLayout {
                    alignment: center;
                    horizontal-stretch: 1;
                    Text {
                        text: root.hint;
                        font-size: Math.max(12px, Metrics.s(14));
                        font-weight: 700;
                        color: Pal.dim;
                        horizontal-alignment: left;
                        overflow: elide;
                    }
                }

                VerticalLayout {
                    alignment: center;
                    horizontal-stretch: 0;
                    HorizontalLayout {
                        spacing: Metrics.s(12);

                        FooterButton {
                            label: root.cancel-label;
                            a11y-label: root.cancel-label;
                            min-w: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 96 : 120);
                            button-height: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 50 : 56);
                            clicked => { root.close(); }
                        }
                        FooterButton {
                            label: root.confirm-label;
                            // The reference's label differs from the visible one:
                            // "Confirm logo" (LogoSearchOverlay.tsx:351), because
                            // "Confirm" alone says nothing out of context.
                            a11y-label: "Confirm logo";
                            primary: true;
                            enabled: root.can-confirm;
                            busy: root.saving;
                            min-w: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 120 : 148);
                            button-height: Metrics.s(card.narrow ? 50 : 56);
                            clicked => { root.confirm(); }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
